meta {
  name: auto-approve allowlist read-out
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/settings/allowlist
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~session: {{sessionId}}
}

docs {
  The auto-approve allowlist READ OUT: schema and map version, the readable tier names, the entries per scope and the folded effective list — decided by the server's own gate so the page never re-decides. Writes go through PUT /api/settings/{scope} with an autoApprove array; there is deliberately no write endpoint here.
  
  Fence: host — Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
